	(text "R401 is a fitted 0R, not a wire. Cut it and the castellated\nUART pads own the bus outright, so a carrier board's own\nhost can drive RXD1 without fighting the bridge's idle-high\nTXD output. That contention is the one failure mode of having\nboth a USB port and an exposed UART on the same two pins."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25 240 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7995a49f-8193-541b-a467-ec267f121eec")
	)
	(text "CH340N needs no crystal and costs less than a dollar, which is\nwhy it is here rather than a CP2102 or an FT232. Running it at\n3.3 V means V3 ties to VCC (WCH datasheet section 5) and the\nTXD/RXD pair needs no level shifter -- only the 3.08 V limit on\nthe receiver's RXD1, handled by the divider on sheet 2."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25 190 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b86acef7-2750-560b-8f8d-c3a00c4bab90")
	)
	(text "SHEET 4 - USB TO UART BRIDGE"
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 25 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.2 2.2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dae1b355-258a-55c6-9833-d82ce9d5a009")
	)
